            <ArticleTitle>Crushing the circumflex stent arm in a case of proximal peristent restenosis after kissing stent for the distal left main disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>351-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case of proximal peristent restenosis after kissing stenting in the distal left main lesion. The patient was treated by crushing the proximal portion of the circumflex stent after passing through the stent arm in the left anterior descending.</AbstractText>
